From acd425ca44538e2bf530f10e2d342408387b086f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Newdigate <nicnewdigate@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 17:59:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] endpoint0: validator alt state and class-request bitmap

Alt transitions plus a set-on-first-arrival bitmap for the three class
requests that constitute a configuration sequence. No timestamps of their own:
the block is emitted at 100 Hz and xscope stamps each emission, locating a
change to within 10 ms, which is ample for a rule asking WHETHER packets
arrived during alt 0 rather than exactly when the switch happened.

The clock hook sits on the Clock Source unit's sample-frequency control,
because that is the request a host must issue to select a rate. A host that
claims the device and never reaches it is the fourth defect this tool was
built for -- and it is reportable only as a metric, never a FAIL, since
nothing in the spec obliges a host to configure a device it has claimed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
