From 00ad1ed542bac48c9a53e9a79bd18d092e231ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Newdigate <nicnewdigate@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:42:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] observer: fix fb_value on the fixed-frequency path, cut
 the block cadence

Both defects came from the first silicon run, and neither was visible from
synthetic data.

fb_value read 0x0 for a whole capture while the host reported fb=44096292 and
a closed loop. Two code paths write fb_clocks[0] -- one under the
variable-frequency guard, one under its #else -- and only the first was
hooked, while this build takes the second. A counter wired to a path the build
does not execute reads exactly like a device with nothing to say, which is the
most dangerous shape a broken instrument can take. Both paths now mirror.

The block cadence divides the fill cadence by ten. The 100 Hz figure in the
design assumed 1000 packets/s; at high speed the OUT endpoint is released once
per 125 us microframe, so the fill probe runs near 800 Hz and 37 words at that
rate is ~30,000 xscope events/s. That measurably dropped data: 10 missing
marks over 220 s and a 158 MB capture, which the judge correctly refused to
report on.

The block carries counters, not a waveform, so a tenth of the rate costs
nothing any rule consumes -- the most timing-sensitive of them asks whether
packets arrived during alt 0, not exactly when the switch happened. The fill
probe keeps its own cadence untouched, because that one IS a waveform and the
drift fit needs every point.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib_xua/src/core/buffer/decouple/decouple.xc | 21 +++++++++++++++++++-
 lib_xua/src/core/buffer/ep/ep_buffer.xc      | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/decouple/decouple.xc b/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/decouple/decouple.xc
index 44a6add0..e7808d2f 100644
--- a/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/decouple/decouple.xc
+++ b/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/decouple/decouple.xc
@@ -157,6 +157,7 @@ unsigned g_uacvPktNotMultiple = 0;      /* word 4  */
 unsigned g_uacvHistSize[8] = {0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0};   /* words 20..27 */
 unsigned g_uacvHistCount[8] = {0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0};  /* words 28..35 */
 unsigned g_uacvHistOverflow = 0;        /* word 19 */
+unsigned g_uacvBlockDiv = 0;            /* block cadence divider */
 
 /* Byte-lane occupancy. or_acc says which bit positions were EVER set, and_acc
  * which were ALWAYS set. Together they identify subslot justification without
@@ -1321,12 +1322,30 @@ void XUA_Buffer_Decouple(chanend c_mix_out
             if(++g_fillProbeDiv >= 10)
             {
                 g_fillProbeDiv = 0;
+                /* Block cadence is a tenth of the fill cadence. At high speed
+                 * the OUT endpoint is released once per 125 us MICROFRAME, so
+                 * the fill probe runs at ~800 Hz, not the ~100 Hz a
+                 * frame-rate assumption predicts -- and 37 words at 800 Hz is
+                 * ~30,000 xscope events/s, which measurably dropped data on
+                 * the first silicon run (10 missing marks, 158 MB capture,
+                 * report correctly INVALID).
+                 *
+                 * The block carries counters, not a waveform, so a tenth of
+                 * the rate costs nothing any rule cares about: the coarsest
+                 * consumer asks whether packets arrived during alt 0, not
+                 * exactly when the switch happened. The fill probe itself
+                 * keeps its own cadence, because that one IS a waveform and
+                 * the drift fit needs the points. */
+                if(++g_uacvBlockDiv >= 10)
+                {
+                    g_uacvBlockDiv = 0;
+                    uacvEmitBlock();
+                }
                 int fill_bytes = aud_from_host_wrptr - aud_from_host_rdptr;
                 if (fill_bytes < 0)
                     fill_bytes += BUFF_SIZE_OUT;
                 XUA_PROBE_FILL(fill_bytes);
                 XUA_PROBE_DRYOUT();
-                uacvEmitBlock();
             }
 
 #if (XUD_USB_ISO_MAX_TXNS_PER_MICROFRAME > 1)
diff --git a/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/ep/ep_buffer.xc b/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/ep/ep_buffer.xc
index ae2ed098..d44dd58e 100644
--- a/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/ep/ep_buffer.xc
+++ b/lib_xua/src/core/buffer/ep/ep_buffer.xc
@@ -772,6 +772,16 @@ void XUA_Buffer_Ep(
                             {
                                 fb_clocks[0] = clocks >> 2;
                             }
+
